+# Current slot tables for local model capacity
+
+The local Minecraft decision service has a real 32768-token capacity. On
+2026-10-12, natural multi-query turns failed with 33592, 33385, 32464 and
+32642 input tokens plus a 320-token output allowance. An open backpack had
+87 current slot records, alongside 37 inventory records. Their repeated JSON
+field names consumed capacity; the observed state was not disposable history.
+
+`decision_input()` now shares field names in inventory and window slots with
+the existing `columns_with_snapshot_index` encoding. Each group has a distinct
+key set. A row's first cell is its original **array index**, followed by values
+in the declared column order. The actual `slot` number remains a separate value.
+Missing keys and explicit nulls remain distinct. Every received item name,
+count, custom name and lore value stays in the current projection. Empty lists
+and malformed rows retain the existing list representation.
+
+`detailsPath` points to the original inventory or window slot array inside
+`rawEvidence.id`. Full observation reads and immutable evidence remain ordinary
+JSON arrays with their exact original values. Existing book-page and opaque
+protocol pointers still target the original array indexes. No new truncation,
+expiry, summarization, model request, game action, tool round, inference slot,
+authority, or deployment parameter is introduced.
+
+Offline comparison using the actual implementation and the deployed Q2_0 GGUF
+tokenizer, on one delivered instruction: 23082 -> 20360 tokens (2722 saved).
+All 37 inventory and 87 window records reconstructed exactly. This is a
+same-instruction representation comparison, not full HTTP latency or quest
+acceptance; downstream query accumulation can still exceed model capacity.
+
+Regression coverage checks every row/value, missing versus null, source
+indexes versus slot numbers, intact names/lore/book/protocol pointers, and
+unchanged full observations/evidence. The plugin suite passed 285 tests and
+49 subtests. This changes only the model-facing projection: a custom consumer
+that previously assumed this projection's `slots` was always a list must
+recognize the declared table encoding or explicitly read the original array.
+
+Deployment and natural-request acceptance are recorded by the companion
+maintenance receipt. A shorter input or an accepted request does not prove
+exam completion, autonomous life, or resolved repetitive speech.
